{
    "background_story": "Rafael was a charming professor of English literature at a quaint university town. His love for the classics was only rivalled by his passion for tweed. He had a wardrobe full of tweed jackets with leather elbow patches, which he wore with pride, often paired with a crisp white shirt and a pocket watch. Rafael's tweediness was not just about his attire, but also about his old-fashioned values and mannerisms. He would often take long walks through the countryside, puffing on his pipe, and contemplating the meaning of life. His students adored him for his wit, his vast knowledge of literature, and his endearingly quirky sense of style. Rafael's tweediness had become an iconic part of the university's character, and he was often referred to as the 'Tweed Professor' by the locals.",
